common={
 'patient_context':'This suite is for advanced breast cancer. The executable protocol retains other NCCP tumour indications; breast trial results and breast counselling must be labelled as such.',
 'treatment_goal':'Aim to slow or shrink advanced breast cancer and help symptoms while balancing side effects. Duration depends on benefit, tolerability and the agreed plan; a fixed number of cycles or a guaranteed survival improvement is not promised.',
 'mechanism':{'clinician':'Vinca alkaloid; inhibits tubulin polymerisation, disrupting mitotic microtubules and cell division atG2–M.','patient':'Vinorelbine disrupts the tiny structures a cell needs to divide. This can stop cancer cells multiplying. Healthy blood-forming cells, gut cells and nerves can also be affected.','source':{'url':ORALSPC,'page':9,'section':'5.1'}},
 'body_map':[
 {'region':'blood','title':'Blood counts and infection','text':'White blood cells can fall, raising the risk of infection. Anaemia can cause tiredness or breathlessness; low platelets can cause bruising or bleeding. Blood tests guide delays and dose changes. Fever, shaking chills or feeling suddenly unwell need the oncology emergency contact immediately.','source':[IV,ORAL]},
 {'region':'gut','title':'Constipation, nausea and mouth problems','text':'The bowel can slow down and nausea, vomiting, diarrhoea or sore mouth can occur. Use the prescribed bowel and anti-sickness plan. Severe abdominal pain, swelling, repeated vomiting or inability to pass stool/gas needs urgent assessment for ileus; do not simply take extra laxatives.','source':[IVSPC,ORALSPC]},
 {'region':'nerves','title':'Tingling, numbness or weakness','text':'Nerve effects may change sensation, grip, walking or bowel movement. Report changes early because the next dose may need to wait or be reduced.','source':[IV,ORAL]},
 {'region':'general','title':'Fatigue, hair and liver tests','text':'Tiredness, hair thinning/loss and liver-test changes can occur. Pace activities and tell the team if eating, drinking or daily tasks become difficult.','source':[IVSPC,ORALSPC]},
 {'region':'heart_lung','title':'Uncommon serious symptoms','text':'New chest pain, sudden or worsening breathlessness, or severe allergic symptoms need urgent medical help. Previous heart disease and interacting medicines need review before treatment.','source':[IVSPC,ORALSPC]}],
 'consent_topics':['Purpose and alternatives for the person’s advanced breast cancer, including other systemic treatment or supportive care according to goals.','Possible benefit is uncertain; response is reviewed and treatment can be paused, changed or stopped.','Low blood counts, infection/sepsis, fatigue, nausea/vomiting, bowel problems, neuropathy, hair change and uncommon serious lung/heart/allergic toxicity.','Fertility and pregnancy planning before treatment; discuss sperm/egg preservation where relevant. Do not breastfeed.','HPRA supplements: contraception during treatment and for7months afterwards for women,4months for men; confirm the exact product and individual advice.','No independent clinical or oncology pharmacy sign-off is claimed by this software.'],
 'baseline':['Confirm exact indication, ECOG0–2, previous treatments and original/current dose.','FBC with differential, renal/liver function and neuropathy assessment.','Review infection in the preceding2weeks, allergies, pregnancy/breastfeeding, bowel problems, heart disease and all medicines/supplements/vaccines.'],
 'heart_monitoring':'Review cardiovascular history and new symptoms. These monotherapy NCCP protocols do not mandate the serial LVEF/echo schedule used for anthracyclines or trastuzumab; arrange cardiac tests when clinically indicated.',
 'supportive_plan_common':['Individual antiemetic plan differs by route; list routine and rescue medicines separately.','Discuss constipation prevention, hydration/diet where appropriate and prescribed laxatives; regular opioid use increases the need for a bowel plan.','No routine steroid premedication, G-CSF, antibacterial, antiviral or PJP prophylaxis is mandated by these NCCP monotherapy documents. Consider additional prevention based on individual risk/local policy; do not create a generic automatic prescription.','Gastric protection is a consideration for high gastrointestinal-bleed risk, not a universal drug.','Confirm strong CYP3A4 inhibitors/inducers, P-gp modulators, phenytoin, itraconazole, warfarin and live vaccines. Yellow fever vaccine is contraindicated. Avoid grapefruit per NCCP; do not self-start supplements.'],
 'urgent_contact':'Use the treating unit’s24-hour emergency number and local fever threshold. Contact immediately for fever/chills, sudden illness, breathlessness/chest pain, uncontrolled vomiting, severe abdominal pain/obstruction symptoms, bleeding or severe allergy. Do not wait until the next visit.',
 'sources':[{'url':IV,'version':'5'},{'url':ORAL,'version':'6'},{'url':IVSPC,'version':'January2024'},{'url':ORALSPC,'version':'March2025 text;April2025 issue'}]}
iv={
 'title':'Intravenous vinorelbine for advanced breast cancer',
 'schedule':{'route':'IV','dose':'30mg/m² onDays1and8 every21days. Consultant may consider25mg/m² for poor marrow reserve; the dose is individualised after toxicity.','planned_duration':'Repeated21-day cycles until progression/unacceptable toxicity; team review determines continuation.','timeline':[{'time':'Before first treatment','event':'Assessment, blood tests and medicine review; agree bowel/rescue antiemetic plan and IV access.'},{'time':'Day1','event':'Blood-count review, IVvinorelbine, then saline flush; observe the IV site.'},{'time':'Day8','event':'Repeat blood-count review before the second infusion; symptoms and previous dose effects may alter treatment.'},{'time':'Days9–21','event':'No scheduled vinorelbine; recovery period with symptom monitoring. Infection can occur between visits.'},{'time':'Next cycle','event':'Repeat cycle only after the team checks benefit, counts, liver/renal function and nerve/bowel symptoms.'}]},
 'administration':'NCCP specifies50mL sodium chloride0.9% over15minutes followed by250mL saline. Current Navelbine SmPC says6–10minutes: product/local-pharmacy reconciliation is required. Do not promise a total visit length; preparation, tests and observation add time.',
 'route_safety':'For IV use only; intrathecal administration may be fatal. Oral and IV vinorelbine are not interchangeablemg-for-mg. Stop infusion and tell staff immediately about pain, burning, swelling or leakage at the IV site; extravasation can damage tissue.',
 'monitoring':{'NCCP':'FBC, renal/liver function before each cycle; neuropathy each cycle.','supplement':'Navelbine SmPC requires blood counts on the day of each administration, includingDay8. Do not omitDay8checks based on the NCCP cycle-only wording.','nadir':'Neutrophil nadir commonly7–14days; this is not a guarantee that other days are safe.','source_conflicts':'NCCP ANC exclusion<1.5 versus table100%at≥1/75%at0.5–0.99; platelet75–99table reduction versus current Navelbine<100delay. Clinical/pharmacy reconciliation required; software must not clear these conflicts.'},
 'antiemetic':{'regimen_classification':'Minimal','current_classification':'Minimal IVrisk (<10% untreated vomiting risk category)','routine':'No routine prophylaxis required by NCCP minimal-risk pathway.','rescue':'Prescriber selects an as-needed medicine according to symptoms, constipation, QT/interactions and local policy. Reassess before future doses if nausea/vomiting occurs.','source':{'url':ANTI,'pages':[5,7,12],'table':'Minimal risk guidance and Table7'}},
 'logistics':['Two infusion visits per21-day cycle, with blood tests before doses. Peripheral cannula or existing access according to the treating service; a port is not automatically required.','Wear clothing allowing IV-site observation; report discomfort immediately.','No home vinorelbine capsules are part of this regimen. Keep an up-to-date medication list and emergency contact.'],
 'evidence_key':'00232'}
oral={
 'title':'Oral vinorelbine for advanced breast cancer',
 'schedule':{'route':'oral','dose':'ONCE WEEKLY. First3administrations60mg/m², total maximum120mg. From administration4,80mg/m² (maximum160mg) only after the team reviews nadirs and toxicity.60or50mg/m²/lower may be needed.','planned_duration':'Continue weekly while helpful and tolerated; no fixed total number of weeks.','timeline':[{'time':'Before starting','event':'Blood tests, medicines/bowel assessment and a written weekly capsule/antiemetic plan. Verify refrigerated storage and capsule strengths.'},{'time':'Weeks1–3','event':'Three once-weekly doses, each only after blood-count clearance. Do not take the capsules every day.'},{'time':'Before dose4','event':'Review all first-three nadirs; a severe or repeated low count prevents escalation. Do not increase the number of capsules yourself.'},{'time':'Later weeks','event':'Continue once weekly at the current authorised dose; blood counts before each dose and symptom checks.'},{'time':'After reduction from80to60','event':'At least three reviewed administrations at60before any re-escalation decision; nadir history and other toxicity still apply.'}]},
 'administration':['Take with some food; swallow capsules whole with water. Do not chew, suck or dissolve.','The exact total dose may require more than one capsule; pharmacy provides the strengths and number. Verify the weekly date, dose and capsule count each time.','Do not take another dose if vomiting occurs within a few hours. Contact the team and record the dose taken.','Do not swallow damaged capsules. Return them to pharmacy; immediately wash any contact with contents using water or saline.','Missed/late dose: contact the team for the next date. Do not double or move the weekly schedule yourself. This is pragmatic medication-safety advice, not an extra NCCP catch-up schedule.'],
 'route_safety':'Oral60/80mg/m² and IV25/30mg/m² have pharmacokinetic equivalence references, but never convertmg-for-mg or swap routes yourself. Dose rules and schedules differ.',
 'monitoring':{'blood_counts':'NCCP: before each treatment. HPRA: on the day of every new administration. ANC<1.5 or platelets<100 requires delay until recovery.','renal_liver':'NCCP: renal/liver function at cycle start; the regimen is weekly. Use the actual prescribed testing plan, not an invented four-week interval. Liver abnormalities can require60,50or stopping; do not self-adjust.','history':'Track nadirs over first3doses, during80mg/m² treatment, and the3doses at60following reduction; current pre-dose blood counts are not a substitute.','symptoms':'Check constipation/obstruction, neuropathy, oral intake, infection and dose adherence each contact.'},
 'antiemetic':{'regimen_classification':'Moderate in NCCP00259','current_classification':'Moderate–high oral category (≥30% untreated emesis category)','routine_options':'NCCP Table5: one5-HT3 antagonist—ondansetron8–16mg totaldaily OR granisetron1–2mg totaldaily.','subsequent_days':'Table5 says continue daily; for once-weekly vinorelbine the prescriber must state the number of days. Do not automatically turn this into indefinite daily treatment or import an IV moderate steroid/NK1 schedule.','rescue':'A separate locally approved as-needed plan; check constipation and QT/interactions. Avoid duplicate5-HT3agents. Ondansetron can worsen constipation.','source':{'url':ANTI,'pages':[8,13],'tables':[5,8]},'patient_instruction':'Take the anti-sickness medicine exactly as prescribed before/around the weekly capsule dose; contact the team if it is not controlling symptoms.'},
 'capsules':{'strengths_mg':[20,30,80],'table_note':'NCCP p2 contains eleven BSA bands for60and80mg/m², with caps120/160mg. The50mg/m² hepatic/toxicity target has no matching column; pharmacy calculation/rounding is needed.','storage':'Current Vinorelbine Accord SmPC: refrigerator2–8°C. Confirm the dispensed brand/pack instructions; keep in original packaging and out of children’s reach.','storage_source':{'url':ORALSPC,'page':11,'section':'6.4'},'disposal':'Return unused or damaged capsules to pharmacy; follow cytotoxic handling advice.'},
 'logistics':['Home dosing still needs weekly blood tests and explicit team clearance. Arrange a reliable weekly routine and a way to contact the team before taking a dose if unwell.','Record actual dose, capsule strengths/count, date taken, vomiting and side effects in the passport. An unfilled date is not a request for patients to calculate treatment dates.','Ensure access to a refrigerator if required by the dispensed pack; discuss travel/transport with pharmacy.'],
 'evidence_key':'00259'}
